  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 145 AM Tuesday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...  High pressure will keep dry and seasonable weather \nacross central North Carolina into the weekend. A chance of rain \nfinally returns to the forecast on Sunday.\n\nHigh pressure will continue to dominate the weather across the East \nCoast of the United States through the rest of the week. While there \nshould be a good amount of cloud cover Wednesday and Wednesday \nnight, it will not bring any rain to the area. Highs will be \nslightly above normal, with highs in the 70s into the weekend.\n\nA system moving across the country will bring the first possibility \nfor rain in nearly two weeks sometime next weekend. Models have \ncontinue to slow the arrival of precipitation, but Sunday and Sunday \nnight still appear to have the best potential for showers.",
